**Reject accessor properties before reading object and array members.**

At `src/shared/jsonLossless.ts:90-91`, the descriptor check accepts enumerable accessors. `JSON.stringify` calls a getter once, and `Object.values` at line 99 calls it again. A getter that returns different values on each read can make the journal record a value that the walk never checked. For example, with `let n = 0`, the object `{ get x() { return n++ === 0 ? NaN : 1; } }` serializes as `{"x":null}`, while the walk reads `1` and accepts it. Array index accessors at lines 38-68 have the same gap, because `value[i]` at line 65 invokes the getter.

Reject accessor descriptors before reading members, and accept only data descriptors.

